# kits.manifest — one row per generated kit. Read by kit-scaffold.sh.
#
# Columns (pipe-separated, no spaces around |):
#   1 kit        directory name, must end in -kit
#   2 label      human name of the agent
#   3 tooldir    per-tool directory created in the project ("-" for none)
#   4 anchor     anchor file path relative to project root
#   5 rules      where rules.md is written, relative to project root
#   6 cmddir     directory for generated slash commands ("-" if the agent has none)
#   7 cmdfmt     toml | md | mdc | instructions | none
#   8 planhook   claude | zcode | none
#   9 note       one-line caveat surfaced in the kit README
#
# Verified Sept 2026. Re-check before changing: these conventions move fast.
gemini-kit|Gemini CLI|.gemini|GEMINI.md|.gemini/rules.md|.gemini/commands|toml|none|Custom commands are TOML with prompt/description; reload with /commands reload
copilot-kit|GitHub Copilot|.github|.github/copilot-instructions.md|.github/copilot-instructions.md|.github/instructions|instructions|none|Scoped rules use .instructions.md with applyTo frontmatter globs
cursor-kit|Cursor|.cursor|AGENTS.md|.cursor/rules/000-project-rules.mdc|.cursor/commands|mdc|none|Reads AGENTS.md natively; .mdc adds per-glob scoping. Legacy .cursorrules is ignored by Agent mode
windsurf-kit|Windsurf|.windsurf|AGENTS.md|.windsurf/rules/project-rules.md|.windsurf/workflows|md|none|Current builds prefer .devin/rules/ which takes precedence over .windsurf/
cline-kit|Cline|.clinerules|AGENTS.md|.clinerules/project-rules.md|-|none|none|Reads .clinerules/ plus .cursorrules, .windsurfrules and AGENTS.md
codex-kit|Codex CLI|.codex|AGENTS.md|.codex/rules.md|-|none|none|AGENTS.md discovery is tunable via ~/.codex/config.toml (project_doc_max_bytes)
amp-kit|Amp|-|AGENTS.md|.agents/rules.md|-|none|none|Thin AGENTS.md consumer; no per-tool directory
zed-kit|Zed|.zed|.rules|.zed/rules.md|-|none|none|.rules outranks AGENTS.md in Zed's priority list, so this kit writes both and keeps them consistent
aider-kit|Aider|-|CONVENTIONS.md|CONVENTIONS.md|-|none|none|No slash-command concept: the skills ship as documented workflows inside CONVENTIONS.md, not invokable commands
